WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.401
-Our next guest
is a very funny comedian

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.337
you know from his work
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.806
which airs this Saturday
at 11:30 on NBC and Peacock

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:10.710
with host Willem Dafoe
and musical guest Katy Perry.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.579
Please welcome to the show
James Austin Johnson, everyone.

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.581
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:25.591 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:32.998 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:35.201
-Welcome to the show!

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.502
-Wow.
Hello, everyone.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.239
-I have a lot of questions
about "SNL,"

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.440
but I want to start
by congratulating you

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.044
on the birth of Homer!
Look at Homer, everybody!

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.746
-I had a baby?
-You had a baby.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.280
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You're kidding me.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.483
-And you posted this
on Instagram.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.085
And thank you very much
for promoting the show, Homer.

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:54.387
-"Late Night with Seth Meyers."

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:57.323
-I also don't think
I even have one of those.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:01:00.960
-Well, I have 47 of them,
and I think he had just spit up,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.229
So I had just changed him
into number 31.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.932
-You got to have backups
with how much they spit up.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.334
So this baby
was born this month.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:13.339
-This month.
He was born January 4, 2022.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.574
Is that where we're --
-That's where we're at,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.944
yeah, yeah.
-And he's beautiful.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.912
He's actually gorgeous.

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.214
He's a very beautiful boy.
-That's great.

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:25.184
-And he looks exactly like
my wife, which is awesome.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.387
[ Laughter ]
Doesn't have a freaky,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.122
long, character-actor beak.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.557
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:34.794
-Working backwards, this means
that you got hired on "SNL."

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:38.398
At the time, that meant that you
had -- your wife was pregnant.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.132
And then, you had to move
to New York City.

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:42.034
A lot happened
all at once for you.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:44.303
-Dude.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:48.508
If no one has ever told a woman
who's six months pregnant

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:51.478
that she has to move to New York
in the middle of winter, I --

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:54.280
You should do it.
You should give it a try,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.015
because that was one of
my favorite conversations

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.483
I've ever had.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.853
It's a perfect reason to do it!
And I have --

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:03.656
I mean, I feel like
some of your experience

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.791
I'm familiar with
because I was also on "SNL,"

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:09.228
but my first year,
I was in like two sketches.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:10.730
-Right.
-Your first episode,

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.364
you opened the show
playing Joe Biden.

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:13.933
-Yeah.
-Which is --

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.835
I cannot even imagine
the pressure of taking that on.

00:02:16.835 --> 00:02:18.737
-That's me.
-It was fantastic.

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:20.840
And now I had heard
you do some impressions before,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.709
but I had not heard your Biden.
Did you have a Biden?

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:26.745
-My Biden was on the list.
When I got here,

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:28.914
they asked me to send them
a list of all the impressions

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:32.485
that I do, and I would say
that Biden was like

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.487
you know, number 38
down the list of, like,

00:02:35.487 --> 00:02:38.190
my confidence level in it.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:42.394
But they had seen a video of me
doing Biden, and they were like,

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:44.597
"Yeah, that may come up
down the road."

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.165
That was, like, what I heard

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.000
when I was getting seen
for the show.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.002
-But on the first Saturday,
when did you find out

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:53.272
you were gonna play Biden?
-Like, Thursday night.

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:54.974
Like, Thursday night.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:58.244
Thursday night, I had one
of those cryptic Lorne meetings

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.379
where he, like -- you walk into
a room, and he's like,

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:01.948
"How do you feel about
wearing pants?"

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.149
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:04.551
Like, he just asks you
those weird questions,

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.685
and like 45 minutes later,
you think,

00:03:06.685 --> 00:03:09.122
"I think they're gonna ask me
to do Biden, maybe."

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.323
-Right.
-It was that kind of --

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.324
"Are you comfortable
with accessories?"

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:15.528
-Right.
"Would you like to wear teeth?"

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.631
-He asked me when I went in,
and I realized after the fact

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.599
it was the meeting
he hired me in,

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:22.601
one of the things he said was,

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.905
"And obviously, we'll need
to see how you look in wigs."

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.807
I was like, "What?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.642
Did you know when you had
your meeting with him,

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.711
did you know he had hired you?
-Yeah.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:35.281
So, they have this, after you
do the audition, you go in,

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.049
and maybe you'll
have a meeting with him,

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.951
and I got called into
one of those meetings.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:42.121
And very mysterious and cryptic

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.523
and warm at the same time
somehow.

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:47.927
And he was like,
"Are you married?"

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:51.330
I was like, "Yes, I am."
"Children?"

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.365
"My wife is five months'
pregnant at this point.

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:54.900
She's about to be six months'
pregnant."

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.970
-"That's a good sign."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.173
"When's your baby due?"
And I was like Christmas Eve.

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:03.075
And then he, like,
looks at the big calendar

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.911
of when the shows are gonna be
on his wall, and he goes,

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.614
"You have a show December 18th."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:12.685
I was like, "Uh, I do?"
I'm, like, washing my hands

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.620
like 30 minutes later, like,

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.689
"Did I just get...?
Do I have to move?"

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:19.691
-Did you ever get an official
call of any sort?

00:04:19.691 --> 00:04:22.362
-[ Laughs ]
They said --

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.863
After that meeting,
they were like,

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.831
"Tomorrow, you might be
getting a call

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.267
from a very important producer."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:31.270
I was like, "Okay, this is it.
I think it's gonna happen."

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.405
And then, I went to a movie
with some friends.

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:35.708
My phone was on like 5%
because that's how I live.

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:37.743
-Yeah.
-And I was like,

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:39.112
"Please, don't die.
Please, don't die.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.213
If this phone dies,
and I miss this call,

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:45.484
they cast me back out
into commercial-actor hell."

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:47.453
-That's a thing, if Lorne --
famously, if Lorne

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.821
gets voicemail, he's like,
"Who's next on the list?"

00:04:49.821 --> 00:04:52.358
-Yeah. Lorne, famously,
if there's one hurdle, he quits.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.492
You know what I mean?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.362
-Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:59.298
-And I didn't get a call.
And then I was like,

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:01.267
I was so drained
from the process,

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:04.704
and I had shot a big thing
for the whole month beforehand,

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.672
so I was like --
My wife was on vacation

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:09.742
with our families in Tennessee.
I was here in New York.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.912
I was like, "I'm not getting
on a bumpy Southwest flight

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:16.181
right after the most stressful
audition of my life

00:05:16.181 --> 00:05:19.351
and just sitting back down
in Nashville,

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:22.121
trying to eat baked beans
while my hands are, like,

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.222
going like this.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.791
"Can I get some more
pork shoulder?"

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:27.626
And I was like, "I can't --
I need to decompress somehow.

00:05:27.626 --> 00:05:31.230
So I took an Amtrak train
from New York to Birmingham.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.933
-Now, that strikes me as even
shakier than eating beans.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.401
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.503
-24 hours in a coach seat
on Amtrak?

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.205
What are you talking about?

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:42.041
You got the guy reaching over
you with his like little cord.

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:44.877
"Can I plug this in?"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:48.281
And so I was hanging out
on the Amtrak train,

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:51.017
and I got a call
from a weird number.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.485
And I picked it up,
and the girl was like,

00:05:53.485 --> 00:05:54.687
"Lorne Michaels for you.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.356
And then he got put in,
and I was, like, crying.

00:05:57.356 --> 00:06:00.893
I was, like, in tears because
I was, like, just so exhausted.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.695
And they didn't call when they
said they were gonna call.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:04.730
-Yeah.
-So then, I get patched through

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:07.166
to Lorne, and he's like,
"Yeah, we got the wrong number."

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.637
"So I think
I've hired somebody else, too."

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.006
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.475
"Where are you?"
"Oh, I'm on an Amtrak train

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:17.776
from New York to Birmingham."

00:06:17.776 --> 00:06:20.213
And he goes, "Oh, what
a glamorous life you lead."

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:24.717
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:25.951
"By the way,
you need to join the cast

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:27.519
of 'Saturday Night Live.'"
-Well, that's wonderful.

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:29.988
You made a great choice.
I first became aware of you --

00:06:29.988 --> 00:06:32.692
I think maybe a lot of people
became aware of you --

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.393
hearing your
Donald Trump impression.

00:06:34.393 --> 00:06:36.328
You were also playing
Donald Trump on the show.

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.397
-Also Donald Trump.
-Yeah, so that's two --

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:39.731
the last presidents.
That's good.

00:06:39.731 --> 00:06:41.801
That's a hot start.
-Yeah, both current presidents.

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:45.738
It's really interesting to --
to play both guys.

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.573
But I think, as a team,
they're doing a great job.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:49.442
-I think so, too.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:50.576
Team of rivals.
-Little bit of him,

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:54.046
a little bit of that guy,
mix it up.

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.615
It's pretty interesting
having to differentiate.

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:59.451
I haven't had to do them both
in the same sketch yet, but...

00:06:59.451 --> 00:07:00.652
-Yeah.
-...with TV magic,

00:07:00.652 --> 00:07:02.154
anything's possible.
-Could happen.

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:05.024
Your Trump is very
stream of consciousness.

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:07.527
-Oh, yeah.
-When did you come to that

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:09.928
sort of awareness that that was
the fun part of doing him?

00:07:09.928 --> 00:07:11.931
-So, I'm from Nashville,
Tennessee.

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:13.765
I'm from a pretty
conservative environment.

00:07:13.765 --> 00:07:15.367
I was raised in --
I went to church

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:17.303
18 times a week
or something like that.

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:20.272
And so the stream
of consciousness thing,

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:24.210
I think I just, as the more
progressive member of my family,

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.412
I remember the Thanksgiving
where I was like,

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:31.049
"I voted for Obama."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.049 --> 00:07:33.619
Nothing.
[ Laughs ]

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.754
So I've always been
that guy in my family,

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:38.657
and so when Trump came on
the scene, ooh, I was pissed.

00:07:38.657 --> 00:07:41.393
-Yeah.
-Ooh, I don't like this guy!

00:07:41.393 --> 00:07:44.196
He's weird, and he's mean.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:46.165
And it broke my heart
for a long time, and then,

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.366
I was a voices guy so obviously
I have to try out doing a Trump.

00:07:48.366 --> 00:07:50.736
And so the first times
that I tried doing the Trump,

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:55.307
it just sort of reflected
my liberal black-sheep anger.

00:07:55.307 --> 00:07:57.509
You know, I mean,
"We're gonna kill everybody."

00:07:57.509 --> 00:07:59.445
You know, I was saying stuff
that no one wanted to hear,

00:07:59.445 --> 00:08:01.647
or I'd say, like,
things he actually said,

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:04.016
and I just remember the audience
just always yanking back,

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.985
especially as I got the voice.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:07.619
As I started
sounding like him...

00:08:07.619 --> 00:08:08.788
-Yeah.
-...and then I would just

00:08:08.788 --> 00:08:10.789
say horrific things,
people hated it.

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:13.325
And you're performing
in noisy bars all the time.

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:16.695
You don't want them to be quiet
with no laughs.

00:08:16.695 --> 00:08:18.130
That means
you've touched on something

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.165
that everyone hates.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.165 --> 00:08:24.169
They're putting down their
Moscow mules to hate it.

00:08:24.169 --> 00:08:26.238
And then, at some point,
I just started, like --

00:08:26.238 --> 00:08:28.574
I realized, like, "Oh, the stuff
that he's talking about,

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:30.676
we got over
hundreds of years ago."

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:32.511
He's bringing up these issues

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:34.346
that we don't even
think about anymore,

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:35.881
so that's when I started
abstracting him.

00:08:35.881 --> 00:08:40.386
I made him like a guy talking
about the wizard on the hill.

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:41.887
Like, I would do
a medieval Trump,

00:08:41.887 --> 00:08:44.724
like a fantasy-movie Trump.
"You know, what?

00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:47.226
The King is doing nothing
about the gigantic dragon.

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:50.328
We've got this giant dragon that
nobody's doing anything about.

00:08:50.328 --> 00:08:52.565
And, you know, the guy who comes
through in the morning?

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:55.500
He does the swords,
and he's banging the hammer,

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.035
and I said, "You know what?
If I could just --

00:08:57.035 --> 00:08:59.972
believe me, this is true --
only I could get the amulet.

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:02.842
Only I can get the amulet.
And that wizard --

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:04.944
We're gonna make
that wizard's head spin.

00:09:04.944 --> 00:09:07.513
When I have the enchanted sword,

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:09.081
we're gonna plunge
that enchanted sword

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:11.751
straight into the dragon's
soft underbelly."

00:09:11.751 --> 00:09:13.318
[ Laughter ]

00:09:13.318 --> 00:09:15.087
And that's when I started
getting the laughs with it.

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:17.990
-Yeah, very nice.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.592
-Thank you.
-Yes, please.

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:24.330
-Thank you.
-You also --

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.465
Like, you obviously have
a very good ear for this.

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:29.302
You made this observation
by listening about --

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:31.570
he makes, like,
weird throat noises.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.639
-Yeah.
I mean, he's been in

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:36.175
the public consciousness
for a hundred years.

00:09:36.175 --> 00:09:37.610
-Yeah.
-We have known him.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:38.977
He's in "Home Alone 2."
[ Laughter ]

00:09:38.977 --> 00:09:40.246
You know what I mean?

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.047
I think he had a show on
this network at some point.

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:45.685
-Oh.
-He's -- He's been around.

00:09:45.685 --> 00:09:47.018
-Yeah.
-We've been listening to him.

00:09:47.018 --> 00:09:49.589
So you have all these
different impressions of him.

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:51.657
Everybody does
a different era of Trump.

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.492
You know what I mean?
And he --

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:58.597
When he came back in the 2010s,
ready to be president,

00:09:58.597 --> 00:10:01.233
his voice
had deteriorated a lot.

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:03.002
Have you ever seen
Bob Dylan live now?

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:04.470
[ Laughter ]

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.206
Like, did I pay for a Tom Waits
show or something like that?

00:10:07.206 --> 00:10:10.942
That's what's happened to him,
and his voice is very gurgly.

00:10:10.942 --> 00:10:14.146
"Hillary.
He goes back here,

00:10:14.146 --> 00:10:14.913
and there's a lot of --"

00:10:14.913 --> 00:10:17.015
So accessing sort of --

00:10:17.015 --> 00:10:20.786
accessing sort of
the dark dungeons of my throat

00:10:20.786 --> 00:10:23.188
was necessary to play this Trump
because he's not

00:10:23.188 --> 00:10:25.524
the smooth '80s --
"She's got beautiful legs."

00:10:25.524 --> 00:10:27.560
He's not really
'80s Trump anymore.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.194
Remember '80s Trump?
-Yeah.

